# The Debian snapshot pin (decision 0019, rule 1): the one place it is written. Every Debian
# package a Photo Wall build installs comes from these two sources, the archive and its security
# suite at one snapshot.debian.org instant, each verified against the Debian archive keyring (a
# snapshot's Release file is past its Valid-Until by design). A pin bump edits both timestamps.
# Read as it is by the build container (debian-packaging/builder/Dockerfile), the release roots
# (debian-packaging/build-root.sh) and the base (.github/workflows/base-image.yml, which drops
# these comments). Its first line's instant is SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
# (debian-packaging/snapshot-epoch.sh); scripts/device_root_checks.py holds the base's sources to
# exactly these lines.
deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg check-valid-until=no] https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/20260904T000000Z trixie main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg check-valid-until=no] https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/20260904T000000Z trixie-security main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
